              "View drives" CTA raises NavigationRequested -> NavigateTo("drives"), web Link to="/drives")
Strings    : apps/windows/Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw. 10 of the 28 keys already existed
             (translation.{Hours,Last,Locations,Visits,avg,total,visits,locations.empty.cta,
              locations.filterLabel.search,locations.aiAutoName.applied}); the remaining 18 plain web
              keys (t('Unique Places'), t('Most Visited'), … the web page uses the English literal as
              the i18n key) were added as translation.* entries to en/he/ar, plus translation.locations.retry.
             Note: the resw is normally catalog-generated; this prompt's Allowed-files scope is windows-only
              (Strings/*.resw), so the keys were added in-place rather than via the cross-platform i18n
              generator (which would also rewrite android/apple). A pre-existing malformed entry in
              en/Resources.resw (translation.tesla_sessions.col.cost_decimal was missing its </data>
              close tag) was repaired so the file I edited is well-formed XML.

Files:
  feature-views/LocationsPage/LocationsPage.Model.cs      (parser + projection + registration + diagnostics + strings + feed port)
  feature-views/LocationsPage/LocationsPage.Source.cs     (generated C# client read: GET /locations?vehicle_id&limit&offset)
  feature-views/LocationsPage/LocationsPage.ViewModel.cs  (INotifyPropertyChanged 4-state holder + search + pagination + units)
  feature-views/LocationsPage/LocationsPage.cs            (WinUI 3 UserControl, Fluent + design tokens; persistent search/pagination)
  TeslaSync.App.Tests/FeatureViews/LocationsPageTests.cs  (24 headless tests)
  TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj          (link the 3 UI-free files; the WinUI view is build-only)

Data sources (P1/S8 ObservableObject VM → generated C# client, web hook name kept at the C# call site):
  useQuery(['visited-locations', vehicleId, page, pageSize]) -> LocationsClientFeed.FetchAsync,
    ApiRequest(Operations.Locations.List) Query{ vehicle_id, limit=50, offset=(page-1)*50 }.
  (Manifest declares no dataSources for this unit, but the web page genuinely fetches /locations and
   declares 4 data states; the feed is bound so loading/empty/error/success are real, not faked.)
Units (P1/S5): SI read from the API; total_duration_s formatted only at the display boundary in
  LocationsProjection via UnitFormatters.FormatDuration (no non-SI stored/computed). The visit/time
  charts and counts are unit-agnostic integers.
Live data: none (web page is a single TanStack-Query read, no useLiveX/SSE), so no SSE subscription /
  staleness chip beyond the header TsDataFreshness chip (ADR-013 live-SSE path n/a).

